  "description": "PROP. CONSTRUCTION OF REAR DORMER, CONVERSION OF EXISTING STORAGE INTO HABITALBLE SAPCE AND \nCONVERSION OF EXISTING DWELLING INTO 3 NOS. SELF CONTAINED UNITS, CONSTRUCTION OF DETACHED GARDEN STORAGE   \nWITH ASSO. EXT. & INT. ALTERATIONS\n\n\n",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reasons of the inadequate combined living/kitchen/dining GIA in Units A and B and the lack of private outdoor amenity spaces for both flats, would cumulatively result in sub-standard level of living accommodation for the future occupiers of the proposed dwellings, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policies GR1Cb and HO2(2)e and Strategic Policy 03 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041), Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (2023) and Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;The application fails to provide any information\r\nto demonstrate how the proposed development would achieve the statutory minimum\r\n10%&amp;nbsp;Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG), as required by the\r\nEnvironment Act 2021. In the absence of this information, the Local Planning\r\nAuthority cannot be satisfied that the development would not result in a net\r\nloss of biodiversity or that it would deliver the required net gain. The\r\nproposal is therefore contrary to Policies G6 of the London Plan (2021), GI3\r\nand Strategic Policy 07 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;The proposed\r\ndevelopment, by reasons of the proposed housing mix, in particular, the lack of a three (3) bed unit, its location with poor\r\naccess to public transport and the substandard quality of accommodation to be\r\nprovided, would not be fit for purpose to the detriment of future occupiers. The proposed\r\ndevelopment would therefore fail to achieve an appropriate housing mix, having\r\nregard to the location of the site and its surroundings as well as the evidence\r\nof local need which identifies a need for larger family sized units and would therefore fail to contribute to the creation of inclusive and mixed communities, contrary\r\nto the provisions of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policies H1\r\nand H10 of the London Plan (2021) and policies HO1A and B and HO2 of the Harrow\r\nLocal Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
